__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
.env.*
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
.DS_Store
# The default `HULLWORK_DATABASE_URL` is `sqlite:///./hullwork.db`, so any command run without one
# leaves a database in the working tree. It is somebody's local state and never the project's —
# and `hullwork doctor` exists partly to tell you that you are reading one of these by accident.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# `uv.lock` is NOT ignored. It was, and that was wrong for an application: the lock is what makes
# `uv sync --frozen` reproducible, and item 051 made it a declared sandbox dependency — so an
# ignored lock means the image is built from an incomplete set and the dispatcher refuses. Caught
# by that refusal on the first real rehearsal, after a commit message had already claimed the lock
# was committed. A library would ignore it; this is not one.
